# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Build contexts: all 15 backend services use `context: ..` (repo root), and
# apps/web/Dockerfile also builds from the repo root. That means the ENTIRE repo
# is a candidate payload for every one of those builds, so local build/runtime
# artifacts must be excluded here or they get shipped, extracted, and (for the
# `COPY services/<name> /app` lines) baked straight into the service images.

# --- Virtualenvs -----------------------------------------------------------
# Root .venv is ~460MB on a 3.14 interpreter. Excluding it is what keeps
# `venv/lib/python3.*/site-packages/...` paths out of the context entirely.
# Both the anchored and the `**` form are required: Docker matches `**/x`
# against nested paths, but keeping a bare `.venv/` guards the root explicitly.
.venv/
**/.venv/
venv/
**/venv/

# --- Python caches and tooling state --------------------------------------
# 124 __pycache__ dirs exist across the repo; they are regenerated on import
# and must never be copied into an image (they can also be stale ABI-specific).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd

# .mypy_cache is the single largest offender: 1.7GB across services/*/, versus
# 32MB of real service code. Because each Dockerfile does
# `COPY services/<name> /app`, an unexcluded .mypy_cache lands in the image.
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
**/.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage/
**/coverage/
htmlcov/
**/htmlcov/

# --- Node / Next.js --------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules (837MB) is reinstalled by `npm ci` inside the builder stage;
# .next (995MB) is a Next.js build artifact regenerated by `next build`.
# apps/web/Dockerfile only needs package.json, package-lock.json, apps/web
# source, and packages/ — all still passed through by these rules.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.next/
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/out/
turbo.log
**/.turbo/

# --- Test / report output --------------------------------------------------
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
**/blob-report/
**/.playwright/
**/junit/
tem/
**/tem/
tmp/
**/tmp/
**/logs/
**/*.log

# --- VCS, editor, agent scratch -------------------------------------------
.git/
**/.git/
.gitignore
.github/
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
.serena/

# --- Terraform provider/plugin caches (816MB, never image input) ----------
.terraform/
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl

# --- Secrets and TLS material ---------------------------------------------
# Dev certs are generated by scripts/generate-dev-certs.sh into
# apps/web/certificates and are bind-mounted at runtime by compose. No
# Dockerfile COPYs them, and baking private keys into a layer is unsafe.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.truststore
**/certificates/
